"tium.t":"⚖️ Tax coordination (tium mas): two jobs — a must!",
"tium.body":"<p><b>What it is:</b> coordinating tax between two income sources. Without it the second employer must withhold at the <b>maximum 47% rate</b> — no credit points, no lower brackets.</p><p><b>How:</b> online on the Tax Authority site (“tium mas” service) — split the brackets and points between jobs; give the certificate to both employers. Redo it every year.</p><p><b>Forgot?</b> Over-withheld tax isn't lost — claim it via the annual refund (card above), up to 6 years back.</p>",
"gl.h":"📖 Payslip glossary: what every line means",
"gl.hint":"Open your payslip next to this and go line by line.",
"gl.gross.t":"Gross (שכר יסוד / ברוטו)",
"gl.gross.b":"Pay BEFORE deductions: base + extras (overtime, bonuses, travel). Tax and contributions are computed from it. Check it against your contract.",
"gl.tax.t":"Income tax (מס הכנסה)",
"gl.tax.b":"Progressive 10–50% minus credit points. On low salaries it's often ₪0 after the points — that's normal.",
"gl.bl.t":"National Insurance + health (ביטוח לאומי / דמי בריאות)",
"gl.bl.b":"Social security and health tax: reduced rate up to ₪7,703, full above. Foreign workers have different (lower) rates and no health tax.",
"gl.pens.t":"Pension / tagmulim (תגמולים)",
"gl.pens.b":"Your 6% + employer's 6.5% into a pension fund. Mandatory after 6 months (or day one with an active fund — retroactive from month 3). No line after half a year — a violation.",
"gl.pitz.t":"Severance (פיצויים)",
"gl.pitz.b":"Severance accruing with the employer or in the fund: 8.33% = §14 in full (nothing to add on dismissal), 6% — the employer owes the difference on dismissal.",
"gl.hish.t":"Hishtalmut fund (קרן השתלמות)",
"gl.hish.b":"Savings fund: your 2.5% + employer's 7.5%. Mandatory in cleaning, security (from the general minimum), construction per sector rules. Tax-free withdrawal after 6 years.",
"gl.ot.t":"Overtime (שעות נוספות)",
"gl.ot.b":"First 2 hours over the day's norm — 125%, then 150%. Must be a separate line with the hour count. “Included in the salary” with no hour tracking is illegal.",
"gl.nes.t":"Travel (נסיעות)",
"gl.nes.b":"Commute pay: mandatory up to ₪22.60/day for days actually worked, unless the employer provides transport or you live within 500 m.",
"gl.hav.t":"Havra'a (דמי הבראה)",
"gl.hav.b":"“Recuperation pay”: after a year of tenure, 5–10 days a year by seniority × day rate (private sector ~₪418). Paid yearly in summer or monthly.",
"gl.hag.t":"Holiday pay (דמי חגים)",
"gl.hag.b":"Holiday pay for hourly workers after 3 months — unless you skipped the day before/after without permission. Working ON a holiday — separate line at 150%.",
"gl.zvira.t":"Balances: vacation & sick (צבירת חופשה / מחלה)",
"gl.zvira.b":"Vacation and sick-day balances: vacation accrues from 12 days/yr, sick — 1.5 days/mo (up to 90). Balances must grow if unused. Compare with “My balance” in the Timesheet.",
"gl.pts.t":"Credit points (נקודות זיכוי)",
"gl.pts.b":"Personal tax discounts: 2.25 base (men) / 2.75 (women) + children, aliyah, degree. One point = ₪242/mo less tax. Check the number on the payslip — mistakes are common.",
"gl.tium.t":"Tax coordination (תיאום מס)",
"gl.tium.b":"Mark of coordinated tax across two jobs. Second job with no tium — 47% withheld from it. Details in the refund card above.",
