"wh.stay.hint":"<b>What it is:</b> the statutory break is 45 minutes a day (at least 30 of them continuous), and as a rule it is <b>not working time and is not paid</b>.<br><b>When it is paid:</b> if the employer requires you to stay at the workplace, the break <b>counts as working hours</b> and must be paid.<br><b>Worth knowing:</b> toilet breaks are always working time and cannot be deducted. A prayer break is not working time.<br><b>Special case:</b> the «one hour for lunch» in a 12-hour shift roster is the employer’s practice, not the law. The law gives 45 minutes; if more is deducted, that is a question for your employer.",
