 "links.h":"Official sources",
 "links.body":"<a href='https://www.gov.il/he/departments/israel_tax_authority' target='_blank'>Israel Tax Authority <small>gov.il</small></a><a href='https://www.btl.gov.il' target='_blank'>National Insurance <small>btl.gov.il</small></a><a href='https://www.kolzchut.org.il' target='_blank'>Kol Zchut — know your rights <small>kolzchut.org.il</small></a><a href='https://govextra.gov.il/piba/piba-services/first-page/' target='_blank'>Pikadon/permit check by passport — no Israeli ID <small>govextra.gov.il</small></a>","prof.name":"Name (for the greeting in the header)","hello":"Hi, {name}!","prof.industry":"Industry","prof.tenure":"Tenure, years","prof.extra":"Other grounds (degree, alimony, discharge) — points","prof.hish":"I have keren hishtalmut (7.5% / 2.5%)",
 "brk.hish":"Keren hishtalmut (2.5%)","employer.hish":"Employer keren hishtalmut (7.5%)","ot.add":"➕ Add to gross in the calculator",
 "ai.t.morepoints":"<b>What it is:</b> tax credit points (nekudot zikuy) are not a deduction from income but a direct discount on the tax itself. One point in 2026 = <b>−242 ₪ of tax per month</b> (2,904 ₪ a year). If your tax is already 0, the points do not turn into cash — they only cancel tax.<br><br><b>Base — every resident has these:</b><br>• Israeli resident — <b>2.25 points</b><br>• woman — <b>+0.5 points</b> on top (2.75 in total)<br>• B1 and 2(a)5 — no base points (exception: caregiving on a B1 visa — 2.25)<br><br><b>For children — to both parents, by the child’s age in the current tax year:</b><br>• year of birth — mother <b>2.5</b> · father <b>2.5</b><br>• age 1 — mother <b>4.5</b> · father <b>4.5</b><br>• age 2 — mother <b>4.5</b> · father <b>4.5</b><br>• age 3 — mother <b>3.5</b> · father <b>3.5</b><br>• age 4–5 — mother <b>2.5</b> · father <b>2.5</b><br>• age 6–17 — mother <b>2</b> · father <b>1</b><br>• the year the child turns 18 — mother <b>0.5</b> · father <b>0</b><br>It is the age within the tax year that counts, not today’s age: a child turning 3 in December counts as «age 3» for the whole year. Points are given for children living with you in Israel; none for children who stayed in your country of origin.<br><br><b>For new immigrants (oleh) — 54 months (4.5 years) from the aliyah date, on a declining scale:</b><br>• months 1–12 — <b>1 point</b> a month (242 ₪/mo, 2,904 ₪/yr)<br>• months 13–30 — <b>3 points</b> (726 ₪/mo, 8,712 ₪/yr)<br>• months 31–42 — <b>2 points</b> (484 ₪/mo, 5,808 ₪/yr)<br>• months 43–54 — <b>1 point</b> (242 ₪/mo, 2,904 ₪/yr)<br>The app works this out from your aliyah date. <b>Special case:</b> IDF service or full-time studies <b>freeze</b> the count — the clock stops and resumes afterwards, so the benefit ends later. In that case adjust the number of points manually.<br><br><b>Other grounds (enter them in the «Other grounds» field):</b><br>• academic degree: bachelor — <b>1 point</b>, master — <b>0.5</b> (for a limited period after graduation)<br>• paying alimony to a former spouse — <b>+1 point</b><br>• single parent — additional points<br>• discharged soldier — <b>2 points</b> (combat) or <b>1</b>, for 36 months after discharge<br>• a non-working spouse of pension age — an additional point<br>• living in a peripheral town — a <b>7–20%</b> tax discount per the official list of localities<br><br><b>Worth knowing:</b> 100% disability is not points but a <b>full tax exemption</b> under section 9(5), calculated separately. Points do not carry over to the next year and are never refunded in cash. You claim them on <b>form 101</b> with your employer — if you forgot to tick a box, the tax is recalculated, but only after you file.",
 "prof.ind.general":"General","prof.ind.cleaning":"Cleaning","prof.ind.security":"Security","prof.ind.construction":"Construction","prof.ind.catering":"Catering","prof.ind.care":"Caregiving",
 "prof.hish.hint":"<b>What it is:</b> keren hishtalmut (קרן השתלמות) — your personal tax-advantaged savings fund, a «second pension».<br><b>How it fills up:</b> 2.5% from your salary + 7.5% added by the employer = 10% a month into your account.<br><b>When to withdraw:</b> after 6 years — the whole amount, tax-free.<br><b>Who must get it (extension orders):</b><br>• cleaning and security — from day one;<br>• construction — site workers after <b>3 years of seniority in the industry</b> (in Israel, across all employers); foremen and crane operators — from day 1. Office staff of construction firms (accounting, HR, marketing) are NOT covered by the construction order;<br>• <b>foreign construction workers (B1/2a5) don't get a fund opened</b> — instead, after 3 years of industry seniority they're owed a cash supplement «chalaf hishtalmut» (חלף השתלמות). No supplement — underpayment;<br>• manpower-agency workers may fall under a different agreement.<br>In other industries — only if your contract says so.<br><b>Simple rule:</b> the השתלמות line exists in your payslip → tick the box; no line → untick (and if the list above entitles you — demand it in writing).<br><b>Nuance:</b> percentages apply to the base salary — overtime and one-off bonuses aren't included (the app calculates it that way).",
 "fired.h":"Dismissal calculator: what am I owed","fired.hint":"A legal-minimum estimate for dismissal by the employer (or equivalent resignation). Fill in — see the full settlement.",
